00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.230 align:start position:0%
federal investigators are trying to  determine what caused a deadly cargo  plane crash in Texas the Atlas air jet  was carrying packages for Amazon's  premiere from Florida when it went down  in a marshy area near Houston Saturday  all three people on board were killed  Kris Van Cleave went to the crash site  where teams are trying to locate the  black boxes just twisted and mangled  pieces of Atlas Air flight 30 591 remain  Atlas pilots captain Rick Blakely and  Conrad Aska died in the crash so did  Shawn Archuleta a Mesa Airlines captain  he hitched a ride on the Boeing 767 to  get to work in Houston his roommate came  to the crash scene super friendly and  happy to be a family man he won his own  family and he got it  for a short time as the cargo plane was  approaching Houston from Miami Saturday  afternoon air traffic controllers warned  the pilots of rain ahead then silence  the question now is why did the plane  end up in a deadly dive the 767 is  widely used by major US airlines and  cargo haulers it's very unusual the  safety record of the Boeing 767 is  exceptional investigators sifting  through the debris were met with  conditions worse than the NTSB expected  the key here is to find the black boxes  they're likely somewhere in this debris  field back here this is what's left of  that 767 it came down in shallow marshy  water we will do what it takes even if  it involves getting in there and  grudging it out  we feel that it's critical that we find  those recorders for CBS this morning  Kris Van Cleave Anahuac Texas
 

